From 629cce488993c565c0bf741a916db36d71a4e843 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:45:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix(trace): keep the code of the error a Java method's
 failure reports

SubsetValue.size and SetOfRcdsValue.size raise their overflow with
EC.TLC_MODULE_OVERFLOW (2178), which -tool output marks inside the
message of the Java method that produced it, as Cardinality's failure
(2154) does. The evaluator of failures kept the reported error's text
in the method's message but dropped its code, so it marked the
reported error only where it was another method's failure. A message
now holds the message it reports, which -tool output marks by its own
code. The front end also told the coded overflow of a set of records
from the plain ones of SetOfFcnsValue and SetOfTuplesValue by a field
written `a : `, where TLC prints `a: `. 23 runs of the upstream
conformance suite that left the reported error unmarked now match: 12
overflows, and 11 failures of TLCEval and TLCGet.
